              "content": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "data": "Done. Here's what I created:\n\n**`config.py`** — Stores the system prompt and model configuration (Claude 3.5 Haiku in us-east-1) so users can easily adjust them.\n\n**`doc.py`** — The Streamlit app that:\n1. Shows a file uploader for PDF documents\n2. Displays a \"Classify\" button once a file is uploaded\n3. Extracts text from the PDF using PyPDF2\n4. Sends the text to Bedrock with the configured system prompt\n5. Shows spinners while processing\n6. Displays the LLM's classification result\n\n**`requirements.txt`** — Updated with `boto3` (AWS SDK for Bedrock) and `PyPDF2` (PDF text extraction).\n\nRun it with:\n```bash\nstreamlit run doc.py --server.port 8081\n```\n\nSince the app relies on AWS instance role credentials, no additional auth configuration is needed when running on EC2/ECS."
                }
