              "content": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "data": "The error means the app can't find AWS credentials on your local machine. Since you're running this locally (not on EC2/ECS where instance roles would provide credentials automatically), you need to configure AWS credentials.\n\nThe easiest fix is to make sure you have credentials configured via the AWS CLI:\n\n```bash\naws configure\n```\n\nThis will prompt you for:\n- AWS Access Key ID\n- AWS Secret Access Key\n- Default region (use `us-east-1`)\n- Output format (json is fine)\n\nAlternatively, if you already have a named profile set up (e.g., in `~/.aws/credentials`), you can update `config.py` to specify it:\n\n```python\nAWS_PROFILE = \"your-profile-name\"\n```\n\nAnd then update the client creation in `doc.py`:\n\n```python\nsession = boto3.Session(profile_name=AWS_PROFILE)\nclient = session.client(\"bedrock-runtime\", region_name=AWS_REGION)\n```\n\nThe simplest path though is just running `aws configure` to set up your default credentials — the app will then pick them up automatically without any code changes. Do you have AWS credentials available, or do you need help setting them up?"
                }
